  "operative_text": "Section 1 (Md. Code Ann., Public Safety § 5-146(b)): (b) If a regulated firearm is lost or stolen, the owner of the regulated firearm shall report the loss or theft to the local law enforcement agency within 72 hours after the owner first discovers the loss or theft.\nSection 1 (Md. Code Ann., Public Safety § 5-146(d)): (d) A person who knowingly and willfully violates this section is guilty of a misdemeanor and on conviction is subject to: (1) FOR A FIRST CONVICTION, imprisonment not exceeding 6 MONTHS or a fine not exceeding $1,000 or both; AND (2) FOR EACH SUBSEQUENT CONVICTION, IMPRISONMENT NOT EXCEEDING 1 YEAR OR A FINE NOT EXCEEDING $2,000 OR BOTH."
}